  <div><strong>Water first</strong><span>Health Canada recommends making water the beverage of choice for routine hydration.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Needs change</strong><span>Activity, heat, illness, food, age and individual health can change total fluid requirements.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Electrolytes are situational</strong><span>A hydration mix can be useful, but ordinary meals and water cover much of daily fluid and electrolyte intake for many people.</span></div>
